---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Me — David Demaree"
  description="About David Demaree, author of Git for Humans: work, writing, and speaking."
>
  <main id="main" class="index-shell pb-16">
    <header class="index-header">
      <h1>About David Demaree</h1>
      <p class="index-lede">A good man, and thorough.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl py-8">
      <div class="prose flow">
        <h2 id="work">Work</h2>
        <p>
          You can <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/ddemaree">view my work history on LinkedIn</a>,
          if you’re into that sort of thing.
        </p>

        <h2 id="writing-speaking">Writing &amp; Speaking</h2>
        <p>
          A few years ago I wrote a book about version control, <a href="https://abookapart.com/products/git-for-humans">Git for Humans</a>, for <a href="https://abookapart.com/">A Book Apart</a>. You can read a sample chapter about making Git commits, <a href="https://alistapart.com/article/the-art-of-the-commit/">“The Art of the Commit”</a>, on A List Apart.
        </p>
        <p>
          I’ve spoken at a few conferences about product development and web design. The most recent one was <a href="https://www.webdirections.org/product">Web Directions Product 2019</a> in Melbourne, Australia, where I gave the opening keynote about <a href="https://conffab.com/video/the-product-polygon/">how we define the shape of the product management role</a> (video requires a subscription; the transcript is free).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
